Iris Malone: Opening a tiny PR to the troubleshooting err-ref focused on 429s/timeouts/context limits. I want one Rust snippet (we hardly have Rust examples), a short migration blurb about Retry-After parsing edge cases, and one stale link fix. @Diego @Kara can you take a look?

Diego Ramos: Love the Rust example idea. Two asks: 1) show parsing of Retry-After both as seconds and HTTP-date, and 2) show backoff with jitter + fallback to a smaller model.

Kara O'Neil: Also call out that the runtime now uses the term 'context trim' (not 'clip') so we should normalize that wording on the page. And add a one-line note to emit a metric tag like `error_type=429` so ops can alert.

Iris Malone: Draft Rust snippet (kept compact):

```rust
// minimal: parse Retry-After (secs or HTTP-date), backoff+jitter, fallback
use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};
use rand::Rng;

fn parse_retry_after(h: Option<&str>) -> std::time::Duration {
  if let Some(s) = h {
    if let Ok(secs) = s.parse::<u64>() { return std::time::Duration::from_secs(secs); }
    if let Ok(dt) = DateTime::parse_from_rfc2822(s) { let secs = (dt.with_timezone(&Utc) - Utc::now()).num_seconds().max(1); return std::time::Duration::from_secs(secs as u64); }
  }
  std::time::Duration::from_secs(1)
}

async fn generate_with_fallback(client: &Client, prompt: &str) -> Result<Response, Error> {
  match client.text.generate("redwood-1", prompt).await {
    Ok(r) => Ok(r),
    Err(e) => {
      if e.status == 429 {
        let wait = parse_retry_after(e.headers.get("Retry-After").map(|s| s.as_str()));
        let jitter = rand::thread_rng().gen_range(50..200);
        tokio::time::sleep(wait + std::time::Duration::from_millis(jitter)).await;
        return client.text.generate("redwood-1-small", prompt).await;
      }
      if e.is_timeout() { return client.text.generate("redwood-1-small", prompt).await; }
      Err(e)
    }
  }
}
```

Diego Ramos: Nicely done. Shorten comments and ensure imports are minimal in the rendered docs. Also add a one-liner example metric call: `metrics.increment("inference.error", 1, &[(("error_type","429"))]);` in text right after the error branch.

Kara O'Neil: Migration blurb suggestion (~90 words): "When upgrading clients, ensure your retry loops honor server Retry-After headers. Retry-After can be seconds or an HTTP-date; parse both forms to avoid premature retries. Prefer incremental backoff with jitter, emit metrics that distinguish 429 from timeouts, and route canary traffic when changing models or rollout behavior. Normalize docs to use 'context trim' to match runtime behavior. These steps reduce hot loops and token churn during rollouts."

Iris Malone: I'll add that copy, the metric call, and a short anchor for 'context-trim' on the err-ref page. One stale link flagged by linkcheck: /legacy/batching -> /docs/optimizations/batching 0 I'll update that.

